HomeDeck ("the Software") is source-available, not open source. The source code is
published so that you can install the Software through HACS, review what it does on your
Home Assistant and report problems. This license explains what you may and may not do.

1. Permitted use

   You may download, install and use the Software on Home Assistant installations that you
   own or administer, for personal or household use, free of charge, within the limits of
   the free plan. You may read the source code, change it and build it for your own
   installations.

   You may fork this repository on GitHub, as GitHub's Terms of Service allow for every
   public repository, and keep your changes in that fork, for example to experiment, to fix
   something for your own home or to propose changes back through a pull request.

2. HomeDeck Pro

   The Pro features require a valid license key, purchased at https://homedeck.pro and
   activated on the Home Assistant installation it was issued for. A license covers one
   Home Assistant installation, as described at https://homedeck.pro.

